 216:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c **** 
 217:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      By default, after the HAL_ADC_Init() and when the state is HAL_ADC_STATE_RESET
 218:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 219:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      examples HAL_ADC_ConvCpltCallback(), HAL_ADC_ErrorCallback().
 220:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 221:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      reset to the legacy weak functions in the HAL_ADC_Init()/ HAL_ADC_DeInit() only when
 222:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 223:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****     [..]
 224:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c **** 
 225:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      If MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_ADC_Init()/ HAL_ADC_DeInit()
 226:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand) whatever the state.
 227:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      [..]
 228:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c **** 
 229:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_ADC_STATE_READY state only.
 230:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit functions that can be registered/unregistered
 231:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      in HAL_ADC_STATE_READY or HAL_ADC_STATE_RESET state,
 232:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 233:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****     [..]
 234:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c **** 
 235:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      Then, the user first registers the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 236:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      using HAL_ADC_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_ADC_DeInit()
 237:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      or HAL_ADC_Init() function.
 238:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      [..]
 239:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c **** 
 240:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      When the compilation flag USE_HAL_ADC_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 241:Drivers/STM32F4/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_adc.c ****      not defined, the callback registration feature is not available and all callbacks
